WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.745
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Proficiency.

2
00:00:06.045 --> 00:00:09.188
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:17.330
Unit nineteen: War, Peace and Memory. In this unit, you will evaluate how societies rebuild after conflict.

4
00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:19.422
peacebuilding.

5
00:00:20.122 --> 00:00:24.989
peacebuilding means long-term work to create lasting peace after conflict.

6
00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:29.054
Peacebuilding involves justice, development and trust.

7
00:00:29.754 --> 00:00:32.348
Your turn. Say: peacebuilding.

8
00:00:35.048 --> 00:00:35.956
peacebuilding.

9
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.265
demobilisation.

10
00:00:38.965 --> 00:00:42.555
demobilisation means disbanding armed forces after war.

11
00:00:42.855 --> 00:00:47.606
Demobilisation helped former soldiers return to civilian life.

12
00:00:48.306 --> 00:00:51.608
Your turn. Say: demobilisation.

13
00:00:54.308 --> 00:00:55.553
demobilisation.

14
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.062
landmine clearance.

15
00:00:58.762 --> 00:01:03.165
landmine clearance means removing explosive mines left in the ground.

16
00:01:03.465 --> 00:01:06.556
Landmine clearance has made farmland safe again.

17
00:01:07.256 --> 00:01:11.011
Your turn. Say: landmine clearance.

18
00:01:13.711 --> 00:01:15.432
landmine clearance.

19
00:01:16.417 --> 00:01:18.556
post-conflict reconstruction.

20
00:01:19.256 --> 00:01:25.028
post-conflict reconstruction means rebuilding infrastructure and institutions after war.

21
00:01:25.328 --> 00:01:28.268
Post-conflict reconstruction took decades.

22
00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:32.700
Your turn. Say: post-conflict reconstruction.

23
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.620
post-conflict reconstruction.

24
00:01:38.617 --> 00:01:40.802
truth and reconciliation.

25
00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:47.542
truth and reconciliation means processes that reveal past abuses to help societies heal.

26
00:01:47.842 --> 00:01:52.558
South Africa held truth and reconciliation hearings.

27
00:01:53.258 --> 00:01:57.304
Your turn. Say: truth and reconciliation.

28
00:02:00.004 --> 00:02:01.829
truth and reconciliation.

29
00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:04.317
war crimes tribunal.

30
00:02:05.017 --> 00:02:09.954
war crimes tribunal means a court that tries people for crimes committed in war.

31
00:02:10.254 --> 00:02:13.089
The war crimes tribunal delivered its verdict.

32
00:02:13.789 --> 00:02:16.755
Your turn. Say: war crimes tribunal.

33
00:02:19.455 --> 00:02:21.095
war crimes tribunal.

34
00:02:22.083 --> 00:02:23.293
collective trauma.

35
00:02:23.993 --> 00:02:28.280
collective trauma means psychological harm shared by a whole community.

36
00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.555
Collective trauma can affect several generations.

37
00:02:32.255 --> 00:02:35.372
Your turn. Say: collective trauma.

38
00:02:38.072 --> 00:02:39.282
collective trauma.

39
00:02:40.283 --> 00:02:41.273
peace accord.

40
00:02:41.973 --> 00:02:45.133
peace accord means a formal agreement ending a conflict.

41
00:02:45.433 --> 00:02:50.219
The 1991 peace accord was signed in Paris.

42
00:02:50.919 --> 00:02:54.164
Your turn. Say: peace accord.

43
00:02:56.864 --> 00:02:57.876
peace accord.

44
00:02:58.883 --> 00:03:01.011
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:03:01.311 --> 00:03:08.082
Rithy, how successful was the 1991 peace accord, in your assessment?

46
00:03:09.383 --> 00:03:15.159
Remarkably so, though not without limitations. It ended decades of conflict.

47
00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.939
What were its strengths?

48
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:24.407
The UN-supervised elections and demobilisation were significant achievements.

49
00:03:25.717 --> 00:03:27.089
And its weaknesses?

50
00:03:28.383 --> 00:03:34.493
One could argue that post-conflict reconstruction was uneven, particularly in rural areas.

51
00:03:35.783 --> 00:03:38.851
Landmine clearance has been a long process too.

52
00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:47.098
Yes. Cambodian deminers deserve enormous credit; their work is, to my mind, among the country's great successes.

53
00:03:48.383 --> 00:03:51.579
Grammar focus: Critical evaluation language.

54
00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:55.364
Critical evaluation balances strengths and weaknesses.

55
00:03:55.664 --> 00:04:02.995
The accord was remarkably successful, though not without limitations. Demobilisation was a significant achievement.

56
00:04:03.295 --> 00:04:06.630
One could argue that reconstruction was uneven.

57
00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:13.074
Critical evaluation weighs strengths and weaknesses explicitly before reaching a judgement.

58
00:04:14.083 --> 00:04:16.770
Now read and listen. From War to Peace.

59
00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:24.387
In October 1991, the Paris Peace Agreements were signed to end Cambodia's long conflict.

60
00:04:25.683 --> 00:04:33.801
The United Nations then supervised elections in 1993, a significant achievement in peacebuilding.

61
00:04:35.117 --> 00:04:40.123
Demobilisation and the return of refugees were complex but largely successful.

62
00:04:41.417 --> 00:04:46.864
Post-conflict reconstruction, however, proceeded unevenly across the country.

63
00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:56.036
Landmine clearance became one of the most important humanitarian tasks, carried out largely by Cambodian experts.

64
00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:04.284
Later, a special tribunal tried senior leaders for crimes committed in the 1970s.

65
00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:11.124
Collective trauma, scholars suggest, cannot be healed by legal processes alone.

66
00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:19.687
On balance, Cambodia's transition offers both lessons in success and reminders of what remains unfinished.

67
00:05:20.983 --> 00:05:23.578
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:23.878 --> 00:05:27.027
Removing explosive mines from the ground is blank.

69
00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:32.896
A, landmine clearance. B, demobilisation. C, peace accord.

70
00:05:36.883 --> 00:05:40.090
The answer is A: landmine clearance.

71
00:05:41.583 --> 00:05:43.780
Which phrase gives a balanced judgement?

72
00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:51.368
A, It was perfect.. B, Successful, though not without limitations.. C, It failed completely..

73
00:05:55.383 --> 00:05:59.775
The answer is B: Successful, though not without limitations..

74
00:06:01.283 --> 00:06:04.017
'One could blank that progress was uneven.'

75
00:06:04.317 --> 00:06:08.040
A, argue. B, say us. C, telling.

76
00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.189
The answer is A: argue.

77
00:06:15.683 --> 00:06:18.693
A formal agreement ending a conflict is a blank.

78
00:06:18.993 --> 00:06:24.098
A, peace accord. B, war crimes tribunal. C, collective trauma.

79
00:06:28.083 --> 00:06:30.652
The answer is A: peace accord.

80
00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:35.996
According to the text, when were the Paris Peace Agreements signed?

81
00:06:36.296 --> 00:06:44.384
A, 1979. B, 1991. C, 1993.

82
00:06:48.383 --> 00:06:51.416
The answer is B: 1991.

83
00:06:52.917 --> 00:06:59.447
Now it's your turn. Part one: What lessons can other countries learn from Cambodia's peace process?

84
00:07:04.747 --> 00:07:10.183
Part two: Evaluate one strength and one limitation, then reach a judgement.

85
00:07:16.483 --> 00:07:32.907
The peace process was remarkably successful in ending armed conflict, which is a significant achievement. One could argue, however, that rural reconstruction lagged behind. On balance, it shows that international support works best when local people lead the rebuilding.

86
00:07:33.207 --> 00:07:35.276
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:36.283 --> 00:07:41.827
Great work today! You learned eight new words and critical evaluation language.

88
00:07:42.127 --> 00:07:46.393
Today's value is love of country. Love and take care of Cambodia.

89
00:07:46.693 --> 00:07:49.345
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

90
00:07:49.645 --> 00:07:52.518
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

